first, pytest checks if it finds the associated fixture in same file. If not found, it looks for the same in conftest.py

for scope="session", pytest will run perticular code once for one execution
scope="function": runs the fixture for every associated function
scope="module": runs the fixture only once at the beginning of module/file. The module/file can contain multiple classes and methods
scope="class": run the fixture once per class(shared across all methods in that class only)

command to run all test files in current directory
>pytest -s

Command to run only test_conftestdemo1.py file
>pytest test_conftestdemo1.py -s

Command to run test_fifthTC function from test_conftestdemo1.py
>pytest test_conftestdemo1.py::test_fifthTC -s

@pytest.mark.skip(reason="skip test")
Add this annotation to skip running perticular test. This is a default marker so you dont have to mention it with -m command while running

@pytest.mark.smoke
this is adding tag smoke to perticular test. You also need to register all the custom tags in pytest.ini file.
to run the perticular tag tests use following command
>pytest -m smoke

